    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-024",
      "what_failed": "Testing DRIVE-as-BEST counter effectiveness",
      "why": "n=44; MDE 0.180 PPP far above observed gap; study could not distinguish true null from effect of meaningful size."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-029",
      "what_failed": "Testing movers' destination net rating change",
      "why": "Underpowered and confounded by landing-spot quality; no usable result."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_establishes": [
    "Pre-move cut share in connectors positively predicts whether their organizational function reproduces after a team move; drive share negatively predicts it (FAM:SF-CHT-057).",
    "The effect is modest (AUC ~0.65, Spearman rho ~0.27) and was detected with n=92 connector movers, still flagged for small sample.",
    "Among connectors, cut-heavy profiles appear more portable than drive-heavy ones."
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish": [
    "Whether the same relationship holds specifically for the Shaper role category (low usage, positive residual influence) as defined in the Structural Influence paper, as opposed to the broader Connector definition used in CHT-057.",
    "That the effect size would be unchanged or detectable in a much smaller subset (n=24 available shapers).",
    "Causal mechanisms: portability could be due to cut-based roles being less system-dependent, but confounders (team style, player skill, role change) are not fully ruled out.",
    "Generalizability beyond the connector movers studied; no independent replication."
  ],
  "own_inferences": [
    "The available sample of only n=24 shapers who move across seasons is too small to replicate or extend FAM:SF-CHT-057; the prior study with 92 connectors already had small-sample limitations.",
    "Even if the true effect is as large as in CHT-057 (AUC 0.65), power for n=24 would be far below 50%, making the question effectively untestable with current data.",
